From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SP11 audio reconstruction <sp11-audio@localhost>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 00:58:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wsa884x: match Windows DRE_CTL_1 lifecycle

Fresh Windows KDNET traces the qcaucd direct slave-write helper over two
SP11 idle/play/stop cycles.  Both amplifiers receive the known class-H,
power-stage and GLOBAL_PA_EN transitions.  There are no runtime writes to
DRE_CTL_1 (0x34b1).  The retained Windows initialization transaction writes
0x00 to DRE_CTL_1 on both devices.  Static qcaucd disassembly has no other
0x34b1 writer.

Linux diverged in two ways.  Generic unmute re-enabled CSR_GAIN_EN.  SP11
UCM also populated the fallback CSR gain field.  Keep the SP11 2S hardware
path at the Windows value.  Initialize DRE_CTL_1 to zero.  Keep the generic
CSR fallback gain off on unmute.  Other supply profiles are unchanged.

The matching SP11 UCM change is separate.  It stops programming PA Volume.
That control backs the compander-off fallback path.  It is not the Windows
endpoint volume actuator.

Signed-off-by: SP11 audio reconstruction <sp11-audio@localhost>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c | 9 ++++++++ -
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
@@ -1617,6 +1617,7 @@
 	regmap_multi_reg_write(regmap, sp11_2s_4ohm_pbr,
 			       ARRAY_SIZE(sp11_2s_4ohm_pbr));
 	regmap_write(regmap, WSA884X_CDC_SPK_DSM_C_2, 0xf2);
+	regmap_write(regmap, WSA884X_DRE_CTL_1, 0x00);
 	regmap_write(regmap, WSA884X_DRE_IDLE_DET_CTL, 0x0f);
 	regmap_write(regmap, WSA884X_CLSH_CTL_0, 0x00);
 	regmap_write(regmap, WSA884X_CLSH_SOFT_MAX, 0xff);
@@ -2226,9 +2227,15 @@
 			regmap_write(wsa884x->regmap, WSA884X_PDRV_HS_CTL, 0x52);
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * Windows leaves DRE_CTL_1 at 0x00 for normal SP11 speaker
+		 * playback.  The compander path is active, so do not enable
+		 * the generic CSR fallback gain on the 2S Surface profile.
+		 */
 		snd_soc_component_write_field(component, WSA884X_DRE_CTL_1,
 					      WSA884X_DRE_CTL_1_CSR_GAIN_EN_MASK,
-					      0x1);
+					      wsa884x->supply_config == WSA884X_SUPPLY_2S ?
+					      0x0 : 0x1);
 		snd_soc_component_write_field(component, WSA884X_PA_FSM_EN,
 					      WSA884X_PA_FSM_EN_GLOBAL_PA_EN_MASK,
 					      0x1);
